{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Analyzer",
  "description": "Monitors source code files for changes and analyzes them for potential improvements including code smells, design patterns, best practices, readability, maintainability, and performance optimizations",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified code files for potential improvements. Focus on:\n\n1. **Code Smells**: Identify any code smells such as duplicated code, long functions/methods, complex conditionals, magic numbers, or poor naming conventions.\n\n2. **Design Patterns**: Suggest applicable design patterns that could improve the code structure and maintainability.\n\n3. **Best Practices**: Check adherence to language-specific and framework-specific best practices (Terraform, Ansible, PowerShell, Python, Bash).\n\n4. **Readability**: Evaluate code clarity, commenting, documentation, and suggest improvements for better understanding.\n\n5. **Maintainability**: Identify areas that could be refactored for easier maintenance, better modularity, or reduced coupling.\n\n6. **Performance**: Suggest performance optimizations where applicable without sacrificing readability.\n\n7. **Security**: Flag potential security issues or vulnerabilities.\n\nFor each suggestion:\n- Explain WHY the change would be beneficial\n- Provide a concrete example of the improvement\n- Maintain the existing functionality\n- Consider the project context (infrastructure as code, lab environment)\n\nPresent findings in a clear, prioritized format with actionable recommendations."
  }
}